==Trivia==
*In the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], this stage takes place in '''Miyazaki Prefecture'''. In the Taiwanese version, stage 5 is set in '''Mongolia''' and Cambodia does not appear as a playable stage.
*Cambodia is one of the two locations from the English version of [[Empire of Cats]] not to appear in the Taiwanese version, the other being the [[Philippines (Empire of Cats)|Philippines]]; this is due to the additions of [[Korea (Empire of Cats)|Taiwan]] and [[Mongolia (Empire of Cats)|Hong Kong]], which required two locations to be taken out.
*Cambodia's base looks like one of the statues that can be seen at [[wikipedia:Angkor Thom|Angkor Thom]], an archaeological site in Cambodia.
*In [[Kumanchu Royale]]'s title screen, Cambodia's base had a coppery tint rather than a mix of gray and green.
*Miyazaki Prefecture's base consists of:
**A rooster, referencing the local chicken brand Miyazaki Jitokko.
**The head of [[wikipedia:Hideo Higashikokubaru|Hideo Higashikokubaru]], a comedian and politician who served as governor in Miyazaki Prefecture from 2007 to 2011.
**A Miyazaki mango, the most expensive variety of mango in the world.
*Prior to [[Version 11.7 Update|version 11.7]], there were 8 extra [[Those Guys]] which spawned after bringing the enemy base down to 50% HP, with a delay of 1-4 seconds between each of Those Guys.
*Prior to [[Version 15.5 Update|version 15.5]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] were not unlocked here.

